*> The world-generation level of the feature stage (docs/protocol/35-worldgen-features-1 section 4; core/src/feat-level.cob). EXTERNAL.
*> It is a view of ONE chunk column, the chunk being generated (CE-CHUNK of contract/copy/CELLS.cpy, addressed by FL-ADDR): reads inside it give its
*> block states; a read of another column gives air; a write outside it is discarded and counted in FL-DISCARDED (the 3 x 3 write window of section 4.1
*> is reduced to the chunk, because the neighbours are generated by jobs of their own: a documented deviation).
*> FL-B-* are the block indices (the number of the block in CORE-BLOCKS, 0 when the table has no such block) the level classifies states with; they are
*> resolved by FL-OPEN for the table epoch FL-EPOCH.
 01 FEAT-LEVEL EXTERNAL.
    05 FL-OPEN-FLAG         BINARY-LONG.
    05 FL-ADDR              USAGE POINTER.
    05 FL-CX                BINARY-LONG.
    05 FL-CZ                BINARY-LONG.
    05 FL-MIN-Y             BINARY-LONG.
    05 FL-HEIGHT            BINARY-LONG.
    05 FL-SEA               BINARY-LONG.
    05 FL-EPOCH             BINARY-LONG.
    05 FL-DISCARDED         BINARY-LONG.
    05 FL-WRITES            BINARY-LONG.
    05 FL-B-AIR             BINARY-LONG.
    05 FL-B-CAVE-AIR        BINARY-LONG.
    05 FL-B-VOID-AIR        BINARY-LONG.
    05 FL-B-WATER           BINARY-LONG.
    05 FL-B-LAVA            BINARY-LONG.
    05 FL-B-BEDROCK         BINARY-LONG.
    05 FL-S-AIR             BINARY-LONG.
    05 FL-S-VOID-AIR        BINARY-LONG.
